## Reviewer points not followed

- sv-a 11 and sv-b 6. A space as the thousands separator is normal Swedish. The checker does not parse it for `sv`, and ACCEPTED-ROUND says to skip it. Period thousands stay.
- sv-a 12 and sv-b 11. The U+200B lines match the Korean source. Promoting Q16–Q20 would also change heading levels. They are not disposable blank lines.
- sv-a 13, in part, and sv-b 4. The suggested wording is the better Swedish. It deletes digits the checker counts against the Korean source (1명·1건, 1명을 넘는, 최대 1배). "1 gång" is that negligence cap, not a surplus next to the 3- and 5-fold caps. "per ett år" was used where the lexicon carries the 1.
- sv-a 2. The suggested label has no "10". Korean 영업세법 제10조 is counted, so "(artikel 10)" stays on the corrected withholding label. The URL was not changed.
- sv-a 4, 5 and 16. "garanti" / "garanterad" / "säkerhetsgaranti" is what the reviewer asked for, and it is the right word. The Swedish pack test bans the substring `garanti` even inside a denial. The denials were rewritten without that substring.

Nothing else in the two verdicts looked factually wrong. The 018 English sentence really is a false label for the branch/subsidiary paragraphs above it; that rewrite was applied.

